---
source: crates/leptoskit_cli/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "normalize(&stdout(&output), &scratch.path)"
---
Signs a source approval for a release you rebuilt yourself from a public commit, after checking that every file matches.

Unpacks the release and compares it with the directory you built from `--repository` at `--commit`: the same file paths, byte for byte. Nothing is signed when any file differs, is missing, or is extra. An approval says you rebuilt identical files from that commit; it is not a review of the code.

Usage: leptoskit codepush approve [OPTIONS] --rebuilt <DIR> --repository <URL> --commit <SHA> --out <PATH> <--release <PATH>|--version <VERSION>>

Options:
      --release <PATH>
          The release container to approve, such as a downloaded `release.lkb`

      --store <STORE>
          The release store holding the release named by `--version` and `--build`; defaults to `releases/`
          
          [default: releases]

      --channel <CHANNEL>
          The release channel, with `--version`
          
          [default: production]

      --platform <PLATFORM>
          Application platform, with `--version`; native releases use a platform-specific channel

      --version <VERSION>
          The version of the release in the store to approve

      --build <BUILD>
          The build of the release in the store to approve

      --rebuilt <DIR>
          The directory you built yourself, such as the `--out` of `leptoskit native bundle`

      --repository <URL>
          The public GitHub repository you built from, `https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>`

      --commit <SHA>
          The full Git commit id you built

      --approver-key <PATH>
          The file holding your approver key. Without it, the key is read from the `LEPTOSKIT_CODEPUSH_APPROVER_KEY` environment variable

      --out <PATH>
          Where to write the signed approval

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
